== NOTES
`import abi::bytes`. A Bytes is an immutable, finite sequence of bytes
with an exact length: not a String, not a C string (a 0 is an ordinary
byte and nothing terminates it), not a pointer or a view. A MutableBytes
has a fixed length and changeable contents, and is a value too: replace
returns a new value and every logical copy stays independent. Both are
opaque structs, compared and hashed by their bytes; only this module can
open or build them. Make Bytes from a List[byte::Byte] (for text,
str::encode_utf8(s) gives one). There is deliberately no indexing,
slicing, iteration or concatenation of Bytes.

