== MODULE
lib/abi/x86_64.bot: import abi::x86_64, then write abi::x86_64::register64
or, as a method, receiver.register64(...).

== DESCRIPTION
Int -> Register64. Written with the two literal bounds directly (not via a
named constant) so hir/range.tcl's comparison narrowing proves `value` is a
Register64Word in the final branch -- the proof the construction needs.

== NOTES
The word is n's 64-bit two's-complement bit pattern, so -1 is all ones.
Never truncates. A provably in-range argument (a syscall number such
as 39) needs no handler; an out-of-range constant is KNOWN-ERROR. For
an unsigned value in the upper half of the 64-bit range use from_u64.

== EXAMPLES
@example accept
import abi::x86_64

r = abi::x86_64::register64(-1)
abi::x86_64::to_int(r)
@value -1
@end

