== DESCRIPTION
The two declared errors byte::from_int's Int -> Byte conversion may produce
(EXPLICIT-ERROR-COMPLETIONS.md item 23): application code meaningfully
benefits from distinguishing "too small" from "too large" (a caller can
clamp each direction differently, or report which bound was violated), so
this chooses the two-error granularity over a single generic OutOfRange --
the smallest useful distinction, not the smallest possible one.

