@topic stdlib.test::Suite
title: test::Suite -- Context struct of module test
summary: The test suite context: the registered cases, in order, installed with `with context test::suite()` and filled by test::value, test::rejects and their siblings.
index: stdlib
symbol: test::Suite
keywords: test suite; test context; test registry
related: stdlib.module.test concept.testing stdlib.test::suite stdlib.test::report

== DECLARATION
    context struct Suite:
        cases: MutableVector[TestCase]

== MODULE
lib/test.bot: import test, then write test::Suite.

== DESCRIPTION
The suite: the context a program installs. Its one field is the registered
cases, in registration order. Exactly two functions declare it as their
context parameter -- `case` (registration) and `registered` (the snapshot
the runner reads) -- and every other function's requirement is derived: a
context implements, structurally, any context trait whose operations its
owner's functions with that context parameter spell (CONTEXT-TRAITS.md), so
the fewer such functions, the fewer application traits the suite could
satisfy by accident.

== NOTES
A context struct whose one field is a MutableVector of the registered
cases. Only test::case and test::registered take it as their context
parameter; every function that registers or runs tests requires it by
derivation, so a test program installs one suite before registering.

